      "description": "Assistant Professor of Communication.  Position: Assistant Professor of Communication Location: Eureka, IL Job Id: 285 # of Openings: 0 Position— Assistant Professor of Communication, starting Fall 2027. Position Requirements: The successful candidate must be committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching. Candidates should have a specialization in interpersonal and/or organizational communication with an ability to teach introductory courses, topics-based courses in the candidate's area(s) of specialty, and upper-division courses in communication theory and ethics. An ability to contribute to our Leadership program is preferred. Responsibilities will also include teaching in the general education program and participating in Eureka's emerging intergroup understanding programming. Candidates are also expected to serve as an academic advisor. Eureka College is not able to offer work sponsorship. Desired Qualifications: Ph.D. in Communication. EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY Eureka College is an equal opportunity employer committed to achieving diversity and cultural awareness within its administration, faculty, staff, and students. The College is intentional in its inclusivity of all persons regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, gender (including gender identity or expression), sexual orientation, marital status, veteran status, disability or ancestry. WORKING CONDITIONS: While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to stand; walk or sit. The employee may occasionally lift and/or move up to 25 pounds. The noise level in the work environment is usually quiet to moderate. WORK SCHEDULE: Normal workdays are Monday through Friday 8:00AM to 5:00PM, including one hour allocated for lunch. Some flexibility for evening or weekend hours is required. SALARY RANGE: $48,000 - $52,000 annually BENEFITS: Benefits eligible positions include a comprehensive benefits package which offers: Health, Dental, Vision, Life, Disability & AD&D insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with employer contribution; tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Click for a complete list of benefits, here https://www.eureka.edu/staff-faculty/human-resources Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
